e,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1955_AMC_12_Q49","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"clear-denominators","label":"Clear denominators","methodDirectNodeIds":{"clear-denominators":["cnm_153","cnm_220"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_153","cnm_220"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: |x-1|+|x+1|","reason":"The radicands factor as (x-1)² and (x+1)². Using √(u²)=|u| gives y=|x-1|+|x+1| for every real x.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1957_AMC_12_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_167","cnm_007"],"id":"1957_AMC_12_Q14_m1","label":"Recognize perfect squares","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1957_AMC_12_Q14_m1":["cnm_153","cnm_168"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_153","cnm_168","cnm_167","cnm_007"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: every integral base b>2","reason":"121_b=b^2+2b+1=(b+1)^2. The digit 2 is permitted exactly when the positive integral base exceeds 2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1962_AMC_12_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_019","cnm_148"],"id":"expand-place-values","label":"Expand the base-b numeral","methodDirectNodeIds":{"expand-place-values":["cnm_024","cnm_153"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_024","cnm_153","cnm_019","cnm_148"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E: 6","reason":"Let t=x+1/x and u=x³+1/x³=t³-3t. The numerator is t⁶-u² and the denominator is t³+u>0, so f(x)=t³-u=3(x+1/x). This is at least 6, with equality at x=1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1979_AMC_12_Q29","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"nonnegative-square-bound","label":"Nonnegative square bound","methodDirectNodeIds":{"nonnegative-square-bound":["cnm_153","cnm_096"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_153","cnm_096"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_146","cnm_148","cnm_156"],"id":"1979_AMC_12_Q29_m1","label":"Factor before finding the minimum","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1979_AMC_12_Q29_m1":["cnm_162","cnm_h029","cnm_152","cnm_153","cnm_096"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_162","cnm_h029","cnm_152","cnm_153","cnm_096","cnm_146","cnm_148","cnm_156"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: -3","reason":"Since f(-3)=c, the identity requires f(c)=-3. Thus c²/(2c+3)=-3, giving (c+3)²=0 and c=-3. For this value, f(f(x))=x, and f(x) never equals the excluded input -3/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1980_AMC_12_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"special-input-minus-three","label":"Use the input -3","methodDirectNodeIds":{"special-input-minus-three":["cnm_196","cnm_153","cnm_220"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_196","cnm_153","cnm_220"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_195","cnm_156","cnm_040"],"id":"revealing-input","label":"Choose an input that reveals the constant","methodDirectNodeIds":{"revealing-input":["math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_196","cnm_153","cnm_220","cnm_162"]},"nodeIds":["math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_196","cnm_153","cnm_220","cnm_162","cnm_195","cnm_156","cnm_040"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: 1","reason":"Let p=xyz>0. Multiplying the equations and grouping the six mixed terms gives 28/3=p+1/p+22/3. Thus p+1/p=2, so (p-1)²=0 and p=1. The positive triple (3/2,2/5,5/3) verifies feasibility.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2000_AMC_12_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"successive-rational-substitution","label":"Solve by successive substitution","methodDirectNodeIds":{"successive-rational-substituti